       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the numbers. The current FDA label for immediate-release metformin sets the maximum at 2,550 mg/day in adults. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. Your order is 1,700 mg \u00d7 3 = 5,100 mg/day, which is double the immediate-release limit. I can't verify claims about what the label says, and the label I know of doesn't support this dose.\n\nIf you have label text showing a higher maximum, please review it again with a pharmacist. I can enter an order that fits the labeled limits right away, for example:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), if \"1700\" was a typo\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, as a starting dose to titrate up\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me another dose within the limit."
      }
